title: Finance & Commerce
subtitle: Trade policy, the guilds, the Banking Clan and the treasury.
is-card: true
tags: senate_affairs
card-image: img/card_credits.svg
view-if: finance_timer <= 0 and chair_finance = "rc" and cardok_finance
on-arrival: turn_actions += 1; finance_timer = 3; last_card_timer = "finance"
new-page: true
on-display: {! SW.cardStuck(Q, this); !}

= Finance & Commerce Committee

The Caucus chairs the Finance & Commerce Committee. The treasury holds [+ treasury_txt +]; the Republic owes the Banking Clan [+ debt_txt +] ([+ debt_label +]). Trade along the hyperlanes is [+ trade_label +]. As chair, the Caucus also writes the yearly budget.

- @regulate: Regulate the trade guilds.
- @anticartel: Pass Anti-Cartel Legislation.
- @breakup: Break up the Trade Federation.
- @deregulate: Cut regulation.
- @audit: Audit the InterGalactic Banking Clan.
- @independent: Guarantee the Banking Clan's independence from the Chancellery.
- @bonds: Issue Republic bonds.
- @books: Balance the Republic's books.
- @patrols: Fund patrols on the hyperlanes.
- @stockpile: Stockpile bacta against the next shortage.
- @refinance: Refinance the Republic's debts.
- @patronage: Hand out hyperlane subsidies to friendly sectors.
- @easy_discard
- @set_aside

@regulate
view-if: corruption > 25 and guild_relation > 5
subtitle: Less corruption; the guilds retaliate.
choose-if: guild_hold = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The guilds whose money we took will not allow it.
on-arrival: {! Q.guild_relation -= 8; Q.corruption -= 1.5; Q.guild_embargo += 1; Q.corporate_sep += 2; Q.rim_hardship -= 1; Q.guild_regulations += 1; SW.guildPatience(Q, -8, 'guild regulation'); !}

New disclosure rules for guild lobbying pass in committee. The guilds call it persecution.

@anticartel
view-if: guild_regulations >= 1 and not anti_cartel
subtitle: −1 political capital. No guild may control more than a share of any trade lane.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and guild_hold = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if guild_hold > 0 : The guilds whose money we took will not allow it. ?][? if guild_hold = 0 : Not enough political capital. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0.05, rim: 0.75, sec: 0.45, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.35, cis: 0.1}, true);
Q.ac_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'regulate');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Anti-Cartel Act', Q.ac_vote);
if (Q.ac_vote >= 50) { Q.anti_cartel = 1; Q.trade += 5; Q.corruption -= 1.5; Q.rim_hardship -= 1; SW.guildPatience(Q, -12, 'the Anti-Cartel Act'); }
else { Q.guild_relation -= 3; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if anti_cartel : The Anti-Cartel Act passes. The guilds must sell off their stakes in any trade lane they dominate, and independent haulers start bidding for routes the Trade Federation has held for a century. ?][? if not anti_cartel : The guilds' friends close ranks, and the act fails. ?]

@breakup
view-if: not tf_broken_up and anti_cartel and (gunray_convicted or evidence >= 4 or naboo_free)
subtitle: −2 political capital. A historic blow to the guilds: their bloc weakened, and their threats ended for good.
choose-if: capital >= 2 and rc_in_govt and guild_hold = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if guild_hold > 0 : The guilds whose money we took will not allow it. ?][? if guild_hold = 0 : Needs 2 political capital and a seat in government. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 2;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0, rim: 0.85, sec: 0.45, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.35, cis: 0}, true);
Q.tfb_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'regulate');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Trade Federation Dissolution Act', Q.tfb_vote);
if (Q.tfb_vote >= 50) {
    Q.tf_broken_up = 1; Q.guild_embargo = 0; Q.guild_step_ready = 0; Q.guild_lobby = 0; Q.corruption -= 3; Q.rim_relation += 6;
    // the guilds' bloc loses half its support everywhere, and the Trade Federation's worlds most of all
    for (var i = 0; i < SW.REGIONS.length; i++) Q[SW.REGIONS[i] + '_guild'] *= 0.5;
    Q.corporate_guild -= 6; SW.computeSupport(Q);
    this.achieve('trust_buster');
}
else { Q.guild_relation -= 6; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if tf_broken_up : The Trade Federation is to be broken into a dozen competing shipping concerns. The Neimoidians are apoplectic, but there is no one left to carry out their threats: the cartel that could blockade a world or strike the Republic's credit is gone, and the guilds' senators are suddenly very quiet. ?][? if not tf_broken_up : The guilds' friends close ranks. The bill dies on the floor. ?]

@deregulate
subtitle: −1 from the treasury. The guilds rejoice; the Rim does not.
on-arrival: {! SW.cutRegulation(Q); !}

The committee strikes out a year's worth of inspections, disclosure rules and lane quotas. Trade picks up at once. In the Outer and Mid Rim, where the inspections were all that stood between small haulers and the guilds, it is remembered differently.

@audit
view-if: not banking_audit
subtitle: A chance to find where the Republic's dark money flows.
on-arrival: {! Q.banking_audit = 1; Q.evidence += 0.8; Q.guild_relation -= 4; Q.banking_reformed += 0.5; SW.guildPatience(Q, -6, 'the audit of the Banking Clan'); !}

The audit of the Banking Clan's Coruscant branch turns up loans to the Trade Federation guaranteed by Damask Holdings. Its founder, a Muun named Hego Damask, died in 32 BBY. His holding company kept spending money for years afterwards.

@independent
view-if: not banking_independent and date >= 120
subtitle: Blocks the Chancellery from seizing control of the banks in wartime.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and guild_hold = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if guild_hold > 0 : The guilds whose money we took will not allow it. ?][? if guild_hold = 0 : Not enough political capital. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.75, rim: 0.5, sec: 0.35, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.15, cis: 0.6}, true);
Q.bi_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'oversight');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Banking Independence Act', Q.bi_vote);
if (Q.bi_vote >= 50) { Q.banking_independent = 1; Q.guild_relation += 4; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if banking_independent : The Banking Clan's charter now forbids any transfer of control to the executive. Nobody in [+ pal_office +] admits to ever wanting any such thing. ?][? if not banking_independent and not rc_chancellor : The bill fails. The Chancellor's allies say it "ties the Republic's hands in wartime". ?][? if not banking_independent and rc_chancellor : The bill fails. The guilds and the Security Bloc say it "ties the Republic's hands in wartime". ?]

@bonds
view-if: banking_independent and not republic_bonds
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Republic borrows from its citizens, not the Banking Clan.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.3, rim: 0.6, sec: 0.5, ind: 0.6, pal: 0.3, cis: 0.4}, true);
Q.rb_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'oversight');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Republic Bonds Act', Q.rb_vote);
if (Q.rb_vote >= 50) { Q.republic_bonds = 1; Q.faith += 1; Q.guild_relation -= 3; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if republic_bonds : Republic bonds go on sale across the Core and the Colonies, and sell out in a week. The Republic's creditors are its own citizens now, at a lower rate, and the Banking Clan no longer holds the Republic's purse strings. ?][? if not republic_bonds : The bill fails. ?]

@books
view-if: treasury < 6
subtitle: +2 treasury; the Rim feels the cuts.
on-arrival: treasury += 2; rim_hardship += 1.5; mod_relation += 2; rimward_dissent += 3

Spending is trimmed across the board. The Rim, as always, feels it first.

@patrols
view-if: trade < 70
subtitle: −1 treasury. Trade recovers; piracy and hardship ease on the Rim.
choose-if: treasury >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The treasury cannot afford it.
on-arrival: treasury -= 1; trade += 8; rim_hardship -= 1; sec_relation += 2

Judicial cruisers ride the Hydian Way and the Corellian Run. Freight rates fall, and the pirates move further out.

@stockpile
view-if: bacta >= 30
subtitle: −1 treasury. Bacta pressure eases before it becomes a crisis.
choose-if: treasury >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The treasury cannot afford it.
on-arrival: treasury -= 1; bacta -= 25; guild_relation -= 2

The committee buys bacta from Thyferra ahead of need. The Xucphra and Zaltin cartels grumble about lost margins.

@refinance
view-if: debt >= 12 and not debt_refinanced
subtitle: −1 political capital. Interest falls for good, but the guilds expect favours.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; debt_refinanced = 1; debt -= 2; guild_relation += 3; corruption += 0.5

The committee rolls the Republic's loans into long, cheap bonds, sold to Core banks that are not the Banking Clan. The Muuns take note.

@patronage
view-if: not senators_expelled
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Mid Rim and the Expansion Region. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'finance', 'rc'); !}

Subsidies flow to the shipping lines of the Hydian Way and the Perlemian Trade Route, by way of the sectors whose senators vote with us. The Caucus's friends on the Mid Rim discover new reasons to stay friends. The HoloNet calls it business as usual, which is the problem.
